        { code: '        CheckGround();', what: 'Called from `Update()`, beside your movement and your animation — the same shape as `UpdateAnimation()` and `CheckAttack()` from 1.6. It runs on **every frame**, and that is not an accident.' , why: '**"Am I grounded" is a fact about right now, not an event that happened.** Nothing in Unity sends you a message when a foot touches a floor and another when it leaves one. The closest thing you have met is the collision callback from 2.1 and 2.2, and those report **contacts**, not standing — a character leaning on a wall is in contact with it. So the honest value is the one you re-derive constantly. The third question of **Asking Versus Remembering**, above, is about exactly this.' },
        { code: '', what: '' },
